## Importing a Role Using Import Blocks

~> When importing a Role using import blocks, the generated config will have to be manually edited to successfully create a Role using it. Read below for more information.

Importing a Role will pick up all fields returned by performing a GET to the API. This results in some properties which are intended to be specific to `user` or `tenant` Roles being read as part of import. For example, for `user` Roles, a value for `default_cloud_access` will be picked up during import and for `tenant` Roles, values for `multitenant`, `multitenant_locked`, and `default_group_access` will be picked up during import. This is due to how HPE Morpheus Enterprise stores Roles internally. When you generate a config using import blocks and run `terraform plan`, the provider will present warning messages informing that certain attributes are only compatible with certain Role types. Remove the incompatible attribute(s) to create the Role successfully.

